      "id": "AC-002",
      "criterion": "docs/07-lane-policy.md codifies the fixed/linked-group membership conflict detection already implemented in GroupTable::resolve (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:127-222) as normative: a package listed as a member of two conflicting fixed or linked groups is rejected during config resolution via GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership (crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:114, diagnostic code E109), with a diagnostic naming the package and both conflicting group names (the group already recorded in `claimed_by` and the new group attempting to claim the same PackageId), before any planning proceeds. This criterion documents existing, already-shipped and already-tested behavior (crates/callisto-graph/tests/config_resolve_tests.rs) and requires no new detection logic.",
