    {
      "id": "AC-002a",
      "criterion": "This spec adds a new GraphError variant, `PrereleaseGroupConflict { package: PackageId, group: GroupName, lane_tag: String }`, with diagnostic code E123. E123 is the next unused sequential code after the highest currently assigned code, E122 (crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:224); E112 is a pre-existing gap in the sequence (crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs assigns E100-E111 and E113-E122, with no E112) and is deliberately not reused, since its retirement is undocumented and reuse risks colliding with a prior meaning. The check is net-new: no existing code in crates/callisto-graph checks for a prerelease-roster vs. fixed/linked-group conflict. It is added to plan_version (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs) immediately after pre_state is loaded (after the block at lines 79-86) and before `aggregate` is called (line 88), before the CascadeInput is constructed (line 117), and before run_cascade executes (line 134).\n\nFor every package in the workspace that has either `ws.config.groups.fixed_of` or `ws.config.groups.linked_of` set (i.e. is a member of a fixed or linked group, per crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:14-15) AND whose bare package name (`PackageId::name()`, crates/callisto-model/src/identity.rs:102-107) is a key in the active `pre_state.initial_versions` roster (pre_state is Some), plan_version returns `Err(GraphError::PrereleaseGroupConflict)` naming that package, its conflicting group name (from `fixed_of` or `linked_of`, whichever is set), and `pre_state.tag`, before manifest, tag, changelog, or registry mutation. This is the only conformant behavior -- there is no precedence-based subordination path, and no configuration can make this pairing succeed.\n\n`PackageId::name()` is the correct key function because it is what the ROSTER WRITER uses: `callisto pre enter` (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/pre.rs:108-114) obtains the snapshot from `Workspace::initial_versions` (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:210-213), whose body is `base.into_iter().map(|(id, v)| (id.name().to_string(), v)).collect()` -- every roster key is therefore literally `id.name().to_string()`. The workspace's own dedicated helper `Workspace::pre_json_key` (crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:206-208) likewise returns `id.name()`. Among existing READERS, the one that matches this writer convention is crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:430 (`pre.initial_versions.get(id.name())`); that is the sole existing read site this criterion cites as precedent. crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:285 reads the same map with `canonical_id.display_name()` instead, which diverges from the writer for `PackageId::Prefixed` ids; that site is explicitly out of scope for this spec (see non_goals) and must not be treated as precedent, changed, or depended on here.\n\nThis check is roster-scoped by construction: a fixed- or linked-group member that is absent from the roster is NOT rejected by this criterion, even though PreMode::Pre still applies prerelease shaping to it (AC-003b case 4a). Closing that residual gap requires the per-package lane model excluded in non_goals; this criterion's contract is exactly the roster-scoped rejection defined above and nothing wider.\n\nThis check runs before AC-003/AC-003b's per-package lane-state check: if a package trips both AC-002a (group conflict) and AC-003 (abandoned-lane gating), AC-002a's rejection is the one that fires and planning halts on the group-conflict diagnostic; AC-003/AC-003b are never reached for that package. This ordering holds because AC-002a's check runs earlier in plan_version's control flow (immediately after pre_state is loaded), structurally prior to AC-003/AC-003b's evaluation, which only makes sense to run on packages that already passed group-conflict screening. A test exists asserting that a package that is both a fixed-group member and on the roster of a lane with `abandoned == true` returns `PrereleaseGroupConflict`, not `AbandonedPrereleaseLane`.",
