      "id": "AC-003",
      "criterion": "This spec adds a net-new `abandoned: bool` field to `PreState` (crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:8-14), serialized as an OPTIONAL top-level JSON key named `abandoned` (the struct carries `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]` at crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:7; `abandoned` is a single word, so the wire name is unchanged by that attribute).\n\nBecause `PreState` derives `Serialize, Deserialize, JsonSchema` (crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:6) IN ADDITION to having a hand-rolled parser, the field MUST be declared with serde attributes that keep it optional on every derived path -- specifically `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"std::ops::Not::not\")] pub abandoned: bool` (or an equivalent that produces the same three effects). The three required effects are: (i) the derived `Deserialize` accepts a pre.json object with no `abandoned` key, defaulting the field to `false`, so every pre.json file written before this spec continues to deserialize; (ii) the derived `Serialize` omits the key entirely when the value is `false`; (iii) the derived `JsonSchema` -- published to users via `callisto schema pre`, which is `schema_for!(PreState)` at crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/schema.rs:22 -- emits `abandoned` as a property of type boolean that is NOT listed in the schema's `required` array. Declaring the field bare (no `#[serde(default)]`) is non-conformant precisely because it would make `abandoned` required in the published schema and break deserialization of every pre-existing pre.json.\n\nThe hand-rolled `parse_pre_json` (crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:43-113), which builds `PreState` field-by-field from a `serde_json::Value` rather than via the derive, reads this key as follows: if `obj.get(\"abandoned\")` is absent, `PreState.abandoned` is `false`; if present and `.as_bool()` returns `Some(b)`, `PreState.abandoned` is `b`; if present and not a JSON boolean, parsing fails with `PreJsonError::WrongFieldType { field: \"abandoned\" }` (the existing variant at crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:144-145, reused rather than adding a new one, consistent with how every other typed field in this parser reports a type mismatch). The hand-rolled `write_pre_json` (crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:115-133) writes the `\"abandoned\"` key into the output map only when `state.abandoned == true`; when `false`, the key is omitted entirely, so the existing round-trip test `pre_json_round_trips` (crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:167-183, which asserts a written pre.json with no `abandoned` key reproduces its input byte-for-byte) continues to pass unmodified.\n\nEvery existing `PreState` struct-literal construction site is updated to set the new field, since `PreState` does not implement `Default` and the literals do not use struct-update syntax. The complete set as of this spec's last_verified_revision is: crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:22-27 (`PreState::entering`, sets `abandoned: false`), crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:107-112 (the `Ok(PreState { .. })` return of `parse_pre_json`, sets the parsed value), and three test-only literals in crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs at lines 1140, 1351, and 1443 (all inside the `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` block that begins at crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:562-563), each of which sets `abandoned: false` to preserve its existing assertion.\n\nRequired tests for the field mechanics: (a) a parser-level test for each of key absent (`abandoned == false`), key present as `true`, key present as `false`, and key present as a non-boolean JSON value (`WrongFieldType` returned with field name `\"abandoned\"`); (b) a test asserting the JSON Schema produced by `schema_for!(PreState)` lists `abandoned` under `properties` with type boolean and does NOT list `\"abandoned\"` in its `required` array (the schema additionally emitting a `default` of `false` for the property is expected but is not asserted, since that keyword's presence depends on schemars derive internals rather than on this spec's contract); (c) a test asserting a `PreState` with `abandoned == true` survives a `write_pre_json` -> `parse_pre_json` round trip with `abandoned` still `true`, and a second asserting the same round trip through the derived `serde_json::to_string` -> `serde_json::from_str` path. `abandoned` is settable only by direct edit of `.changeset/pre.json` (no CLI support is added by this spec, per non_goals).\n\nFor a given package, evaluated only after that package has cleared AC-002a's group-conflict check (a package rejected by AC-002a is never evaluated against this criterion), the sole discriminator for the gate below is `pre_state.abandoned` -- not `PreMode`, and not any new `VersionOptions` field (see non_goals for why no such field is introduced). Immediately after AC-002a's check in plan_version, for every package whose bare name (`PackageId::name()`) is a key in the active `pre_state.initial_versions` roster (pre_state is Some) and `pre_state.abandoned == true`, plan_version returns `Err(GraphError::AbandonedPrereleaseLane { package: PackageId, lane_tag: String })` (a new GraphError variant, diagnostic code E124, the next sequential code after AC-002a's E123), naming the package and `pre_state.tag`, with a diagnostic/help message directing the operator to clear the abandoned lane (delete .changeset/pre.json, or edit `abandoned` back to `false` or remove the key) before planning can proceed, before manifest, tag, changelog, or registry mutation. This holds regardless of `PreMode` (Pre or Exit) -- an abandoned lane is blocked in either mode, since neither accumulating further prereleases nor finalizing to stable is a sensible operation on a lane the operator has marked abandoned. A test exists asserting this rejection for a package on the roster with `abandoned == true`, in both PreMode::Pre and PreMode::Exit.",
      "is_error_case": true
