    {
      "id": "AC-003b",
      "criterion": "Given a package that cleared AC-002a (no group conflict) and is not rejected by AC-003 (`pre_state.abandoned` is not `true`), plan_version permits planning to proceed in every one of the following starting states, with no new rejection introduced by this spec. Each state's described outcome is already-shipped behavior that this criterion codifies as normative and intended, not new logic; an automated test exists for each state asserting plan_version returns `Ok` and asserting the stated version shape.\n\n(1) NO LANE ACTIVE -- `.changeset/pre.json` does not exist (`pre_state` is `None`). Planning proceeds using ordinary independent/group severity inference, unaffected by any lane: no synthetic-severity injection runs (the block at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:104-115 is guarded by `if let Some(ref pre) = pre_state`), and `bump_target` takes its no-lane branch (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:441-443, `versioning.bump(&base, sev)`). Test asserts a package with a Minor changeset bumps to the ordinary stable Minor target.\n\n(2) LANE ACTIVE, PACKAGE ON ROSTER, `abandoned == false`, `mode == PreMode::Pre`. Planning proceeds and produces a prerelease-tagged bump: `bump_target` takes the Pre branch (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:429-433) and computes `pinned_base = pre.initial_versions.get(id.name())`, which for a roster member resolves to the lane-entry snapshot, then calls `bump_prerelease(pinned_base, sev, &pre.tag, &base)`. The lane is actively accumulating, and continuing to accumulate is its normal, expected operation, not a condition to block. Test asserts the resulting bump carries a prerelease-tagged version bearing `pre_state.tag`.\n\n(3) LANE ACTIVE, PACKAGE ON ROSTER, `abandoned == false`, `mode == PreMode::Exit`. Planning proceeds and finalizes the package's prerelease version to stable: the synthetic-severity-injection loop (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:104-115) gives the package `Severity::Patch` + `BumpReason::PreRelease` if it has no severity already, and `bump_target` takes the Exit branch (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:434-440, `versioning.bump(&base, sev)`), which strips the prerelease tag. Test asserts the resulting bump carries a finalized stable version.\n\n(4a) LANE ACTIVE, PACKAGE NOT ON ROSTER, `mode == PreMode::Pre`. Planning proceeds -- there is no rejection -- but, contrary to what off-roster status might suggest, the lane DOES influence this package's version shape. `bump_target` (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:412-444) receives the workspace-scoped `input.pre` (set from `pre_state.as_ref()` at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:125) and its Pre branch at crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:429 is entered for EVERY package it is called on, with no roster check anywhere in the function. Consequently: if the off-roster package has a non-None severity from ordinary changeset or inference sources, it receives a PRERELEASE-TAGGED bump bearing `pre_state.tag`, exactly as a roster member would; the only roster-sensitive difference is the baseline, since `pre.initial_versions.get(id.name())` misses and `.unwrap_or(&base)` (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:430) falls back to the package's own live on-disk version instead of a lane-entry snapshot. If the package has severity `Severity::None`, it is not bumped at all, the same as any unbumped package. THIS STATE IS THEREFORE NOT IDENTICAL TO CASE (1). This is declared INTENDED normative behavior, not a defect: while a workspace is in PreMode::Pre, every version the planner emits is a prerelease by design, and the roster's documented purpose is to pin baselines (see the shipped test `test_bump_target_uses_pinned_pre_baseline_not_current_prerelease` and its doc comment at crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:1413-1419), not to gate tagging. Restricting shaping to roster members would require the per-package lane model excluded in non_goals. Test: with a lane active in PreMode::Pre whose roster contains only package A, a package B that is absent from the roster and carries a Minor changeset must plan to a prerelease-tagged version bearing `pre_state.tag`, and its prerelease baseline must be B's own on-disk base version rather than any roster entry.\n\n(4b) LANE ACTIVE, PACKAGE NOT ON ROSTER, `mode == PreMode::Exit`. Planning proceeds -- there is no rejection -- and the synthetic-severity-injection loop applies to this package IF AND ONLY IF its base version satisfies `is_prerelease()`. The loop at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:106 is `for (id, ver) in &base_versions`, i.e. it iterates every package in the workspace, and its only filter is `if ver.is_prerelease()` at line 107 -- there is no roster-membership condition. Therefore: an off-roster package whose base version IS a prerelease receives the synthetic `Severity::Patch` + `BumpReason::PreRelease { tag }` (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:108-111) and is finalized to a stable version by the Exit branch at crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:439, despite never having been on the roster. An off-roster package whose base version is STABLE receives no injection, and if it has a real severity from a changeset the Exit branch's `versioning.bump(&base, sev)` (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:439) is textually and behaviorally identical to the no-lane branch (crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:442), so it behaves identically to case (1). This is declared INTENDED normative behavior, not a defect: the injection is genuinely severity-based (finalize anything that is currently at a prerelease version), not membership-based, which is the correct semantics for exiting a workspace-scoped prerelease cycle -- a package that was tagged into a prerelease during the cycle must be finalized on exit whether or not it was on the roster at `pre enter` time, otherwise it would be stranded at a prerelease version forever. Test (two assertions, both with a lane active in PreMode::Exit whose roster contains only package A): a package B absent from the roster whose on-disk version is `1.2.0-next.3` must plan to the finalized stable `1.2.0`; and a package C absent from the roster whose on-disk version is the stable `2.0.0` and which carries a Minor changeset must plan to `2.1.0`, the identical result the same fixture produces with no pre.json present.",
