  "revision_note": "Round-4 correction of three canon:exit-gate blockers, with every code citation re-verified by reading the named file at revision 39b250ae rather than carried over from a prior round.\n\nBLOCKER 1 (AC-003b case 4 factually wrong) -- FIXED, but NOT as the blocker prescribed. Case (4) is split into (4a) PreMode::Pre and (4b) PreMode::Exit as instructed, and (4b) is written exactly as instructed: the injection loop at crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:106-107 iterates all of base_versions filtering only on `ver.is_prerelease()`, so an off-roster prerelease-versioned package IS finalized; declared intended, with the required two-shape test (prerelease-versioned and stable-versioned off-roster packages). However, the blocker's prescribed text for (4a) -- 'proceeds identically to case (1), no lane influence' -- is itself factually wrong and was NOT adopted. crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:428-433 shows `bump_target` entering its PreMode::Pre branch for every package it is called on, with the roster consulted only at line 430 as `pre.initial_versions.get(id.name()).unwrap_or(&base)` -- a BASELINE lookup with a fallback, not a membership gate. An off-roster package with any non-None severity therefore still receives a prerelease-tagged bump in PreMode::Pre; only its prerelease baseline differs. (4a) now states that accurately, declares it intended, and carries a test asserting the prerelease tag AND the live-base fallback.\n\nBLOCKER 2 (abandoned field would become schema-required) -- FIXED as instructed. Verified crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/schema.rs:22 is `\"pre\" => schema_for!(PreState)` and crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:6 derives Serialize, Deserialize, AND JsonSchema alongside the hand-rolled parser -- so the prior draft's claim that the derive path is irrelevant was wrong. AC-003 now mandates `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"std::ops::Not::not\")]`, enumerates the three required effects, and adds the schema-`required` test and both round-trip tests. Construction sites were re-derived from the current tree, not reused: crates/callisto-format/src/pre.rs:22-27 and :107-112, plus three test-only literals at crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:1140, :1351, and :1443 (all inside the `#[cfg(test)]` block starting at :562).\n\nBLOCKER 3 (false AC-002a citation) -- FIXED as instructed. Verified crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs:285 uses `canonical_id.display_name()`, not `name()`, and crates/callisto-model/src/identity.rs:84-107 confirms the two diverge for PackageId::Prefixed. AC-002a now cites only crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:430 as the matching reader, and grounds the choice on the WRITER: crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:210-213 (`Workspace::initial_versions`) keys with `id.name().to_string()`, reached from `callisto pre enter` at crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/pre.rs:108-114; `Workspace::pre_json_key` at crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:206-208 corroborates. A new non_goals entry records aggregate.rs:285's divergence as out of scope and explicitly not sanctioned.\n\nTWO ADDITIONAL FALSE CITATIONS found and fixed while verifying, neither reported by the gate: (a) AC-001 referenced a `claimed_by`-versus-`ungrouped` distinction, but no `ungrouped` identifier exists anywhere in crates/ -- independence is now defined as the absence of both `fixed_of` and `linked_of` entries (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:14-15), and every claimed_by line number is now individually cited. (b) AC-004 named a fixture test `test_plan_version_produces_correct_bumps_in_cascade` that does not exist in crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs; it now names the real `plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_bumped_owner_with_platform_sibling` at :699-702.\n\nAlso reconciled: the non_goals entry that described `initial_versions` as the lane's 'membership' now correctly describes it as a ROSTER that pins baselines and scopes AC-002a/AC-003's checks but does not gate prerelease shaping, and AC-001 gained an explicit carve-out distinguishing version AUTHORITY (selects severity and baseline) from workspace-wide prerelease SHAPING (applies a tag to an already-selected result), so AC-001's 'MUST NOT apply concurrently' for pairs (5)/(6) no longer silently contradicts AC-003b (4a). AC-002a now states outright that an off-roster group member is not rejected and that closing that residual gap is excluded by non_goals."
